# make-skill — ship skills the proven way (Cursor)

Self-contained rule (Cursor copies this into projects — no external links).

## Authoring rules (every skill)

- Front-matter: `name` == directory name; `description` starts "Use when …" with
  concrete trigger phrases in English AND Russian. A skill nobody triggers is dead
  weight.
- One skill = one job. Multiple concerns → multiple skills + a shared contract file.
- Body: imperative, procedural, checklists over prose. State non-negotiables as such.
- Commands are thin wrappers: front-matter `description` (+ `argument-hint`), body =
  "invoke skill X in mode Y", pass `$ARGUMENTS`.
- Never overwrite user data: seed only when absent; overwrite only behind `--force`.

## Distributable repo layout

```
.claude-plugin/marketplace.json            # plugins[0].source: ./plugins/<name>
plugins/<name>/.claude-plugin/plugin.json
plugins/<name>/commands/*.md
plugins/<name>/skills/<skill>/SKILL.md (+ references/*.md)
cursor/rules/*.mdc                         # self-contained, NO relative links
templates/*.md                             # skeletons seeded into projects
bin/<name>.js + package.json               # zero-dep npx installer
test/validate.py                           # stdlib-only consistency validator
.github/workflows/validate.yml (+ release.yml, off by default)
install.sh, README.md (EN+RU), CHANGELOG.md, LICENSE (MIT)
docs/superpowers/{specs,plans}/
```

## Hard rules

- **Version sync:** marketplace.json, plugin.json, package.json (if npm), and the
  top CHANGELOG entry carry the SAME semver, bumped together; the validator enforces.
- **Validator must be able to fail:** CI runs a negative self-test (corrupt a copy →
  expect FAIL). A validator that can't fail is decoration.
- **One channel per agent:** don't run a plugin AND a plain `~/.claude/skills` copy
  on the same install — the stale plain copy shadows the plugin.
- **npm name first:** `npm view <name>` (E404 = free). **npm publish = human 2FA.**
- **Cursor .mdc:** embed contracts inline (files get copied into foreign projects).
- **e2e npx from a NON-repo cwd** (inside the repo it resolves the local package →
  false "command not found").

## Distribution

Claude Code plugin (`claude plugin marketplace add` → `install <name>@<name>`),
vercel skills CLI (`npx skills add <owner>/<repo>`, discovers via marketplace.json),
npx (`npx github:<owner>/<repo>`, or the registry after publish), Cursor (global via
`npx skills add … --agent cursor --global`, or per-project `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`).
